<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21071] ll_fsync() does not mark writeback errors as seen</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21071</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When dirty pages are discarded, for example on eviction, vvp_vmpage_error() records -EIO in mapping -&amp;gt;wb_err with mapping_set_error().&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ll_fsync() only calls filemap_write_and_wait_range(). It never calls file_check_and_advance_wb_err(), so the error is never marked as seen (ERRSEQ_SEEN).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because the error is never seen, errseq_sample() returns 0 for every new open of the inode. filemap_check_wb_err() then reports the same old error again, on every open, until the inode is evicted from the cache.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This causes problems for a Lustre client re-exported with NFS. knfsd closes and reopens files often (filecache GC), so it sees the error each time and calls nfsd_reset_write_verifier(). The write verifier changes every few seconds, and NFS clients must resend all uncommitted writes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How to reproduce:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. Write to a file on a Lustre client that is exported by knfsd.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Evict the client while it has dirty pages:&lt;br/&gt;
   lctl set_param obdfilter.*.evict_client=nid:&amp;lt;client nid&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
3. Keep the file open and closed through NFS. The write verifier changes again and again, and NFS writes to the file get EIO.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;echo 3 &amp;gt; /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches together with lctl set_param ldlm.namespaces.*.lru_size=clear stops it, because both evict the inode.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description>
